# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).

## [Unreleased]

### Added
  - `CaptureStats` (`core::stats`): running capture statistics (packet count,
    bytes, first/last timestamp) computed in constant memory
  - `PcapError::Truncated`: a capture that ends in the middle of a packet is
    reported as truncated instead of a generic read error
  - `PacketId` (`core::packet`): identity of a packet, its position in the
    capture numbered from 1 like Wireshark frame numbers; `RawPacket::id()`
  - `protocols` module, with the protocol number types `EtherType` and
    `IpProtocol` (known values as constants, e.g. `IpProtocol::TCP`)
  - `Span` (`protocols`): position of a header in the raw bytes of its packet
  - `Stop` and `HeaderKind` (`protocols`): why decoding of a packet ended early
    (truncated, malformed, unsupported protocol, too many nested headers)
  - `LinkType` implements `Hash`
  - `Header` (`protocols`): a decoded header, one variant per protocol;
    `Ethernet` header and `MacAddr`
  - `RawPacket::decode()` returns a `Packet` (`protocols`): packet metadata and
    its decoded headers, outermost first, plus why decoding stopped early;
    at most `MAX_DEPTH` (16) headers per packet
  - `RawPacket::link_type()`
  - `ProtocolStats` (`protocols`): headers decoded by kind and packets stopped
    early by reason, most frequent first
  - `onx packets stats` (`onx p s`): decode every packet of a capture and print
    protocol statistics
  - `HeaderKind`, `Stop` and `LinkType` implement `PartialOrd` and `Ord`
  - `Ipv4` header (`Header::Ipv4`) and `Fragment`, the position of an IP packet
    in a fragmented datagram
  - `RawPacket::decode()` decodes IPv4 headers (options included in the span);
    a non-first fragment ends decoding normally, without a `Stop`
  - `Ipv6` header (`Header::Ipv6`): the fixed header; extension headers will be
    separate headers in the stack
  - `RawPacket::decode()` decodes the IPv6 fixed header; extension headers are
    reported as unsupported for now
  - `Ipv6Fragment` header (`Header::Ipv6Fragment`, `HeaderKind::Ipv6Fragment`):
    the IPv6 Fragment extension header
  - `IpProtocol` constants for the IPv6 extension headers (`IPV6_HOPOPT`,
    `IPV6_ROUTE`, `IPV6_FRAG`, `IPV6_OPTS`) and `IPV6_NONXT`
  - `EtherType::ARP` and `IpProtocol::IGMP` constants (shown by name in
    `onx packets stats`)

### Fixed
  - `onx read` streams packets instead of loading the whole capture in memory
    (1 GB capture: peak RSS 1.19 GB -> 10 MB)
  - `onx read` keeps and reports the packets read before an error, then exits
    with status 1, instead of discarding them
  - A missing or unreadable capture file is reported as an I/O error instead
    of "Unsupported file format"; the file is opened once instead of three times
  - `onx packets stats` aligns its counts whatever the length of the labels

### Changed
  - **Breaking:** `NxPacket` renamed to `RawPacket`, `NxPacketFormat` to `DisplayFormat`,
    `NxPacketDisplay` to `RawPacketDisplay`. Library types no longer carry the `Nx`
    prefix: modules namespace them (`onx::core::packet::RawPacket`).
  - **Breaking:** `RawPacket::new` takes a `PacketId` as its first argument.
  - **Breaking (CLI):** commands are grouped by object (`onx <group> <command>`),
    each with a short alias. `onx read` is now `onx capture info` (`onx c i`).
    The CLI is unstable during 0.0.x.
  - CLI help describes every command and argument.
  - **Breaking:** `PcapError` and `LinkType` are `#[non_exhaustive]`: a `match`
    on them outside onx needs a wildcard arm, so variants can be added later
    without a breaking change.

### Removed
  - **Breaking:** `PcapSource::is_pcap_file` and `PcapNgSource::is_pcapng_file`.
    They returned `false` for a file that could not be read; use
    `read_capture_file`, which detects the format and reports I/O errors.

### Dependencies
  - Added etherparse 0.21.0 (used privately: no etherparse type in the public API)
  - Added arrayvec 0.7.8 (already a dependency of etherparse; not exposed in the
    public API)

## [0.0.2] - 2026-02-15

### Added
  - PCAP and PCAPNG file reading
  - `NxPacket` struct for unified packet representation
  - `PacketSource` trait for capture abstraction
  - Basic CLI with `read` command
  - Integration tests with sample PCAP files
  
  ### Dependencies
  - Added pcap-file 3.0.0-rc1
  - Added thiserror 2.0.18
  - Added clap 4.5
  - Added time 0.3

## [0.0.1] - 2026-01-31

### Added
- Initial project structure
- Workspace setup with `onx` crate
- MIT OR Apache-2.0 dual licensing
- Placeholder binary for crate name reservation

### Notes
This is a name reservation release. Core functionality will be implemented
in v0.1.0.
